        <item>
            <title>0.1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:08:59 -0700</pubDate>
            <link>https://freeside.banast.as</link>
            <sparkle:version>1</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>27.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>The first preview release.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Free space for external drives, disk images, network shares and the internal disk, matching Finder, with a mark when a volume runs low</li>
  <li>Read and write rates for each physical drive, with a 60-second trace and session totals</li>
  <li>Eject and Eject All, done the way Finder does; when a drive won't eject, a list of the apps and processes holding it and the files they have open, with Quit, Terminate, Retry and Force Eject</li>
  <li>"Who's using this?" for any drive, without ejecting</li>
  <li>Menu bar shows a drive icon, free space on one volume, live rates, or both, and switches to rates during a copy</li>
  <li>Optional notifications for low space and for a finished copy of 1 GB or more</li>
  <li>Copy Diagnostics for bug reports, with no file paths in it</li>
  <li>Signed, notarized and updated automatically</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
